00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:07.190 align:start position:0%
eu ministers meeting in the  competitiveness council on thursday and  friday recognized the central importance  of industry for boosting competitiveness  and sustainable growth in europe  they agreed on the need to intensify  efforts to mainstream industrial  competitiveness across all policy areas  such as environment climate energy trade  and regional policies  ministers also outlined the importance  of breaking down barriers to industrial  competitiveness such as high energy  bills in europe  we aim to address the high cost  of energy and the lack of a unified  energy market  i believe that this is  probably the most important  priority  ministers also reviewed the commission's  annual growth survey for 2014 which is  the starting point of the european  semester in order to encourage growth  and competitiveness the council stressed  that efforts need to continue in  priority areas such as fiscal  consolidation restoring normal lending  to the economy tackling unemployment and  modernizing public administrations  on the implementation of the european  research area ministers believe that  although much has already been achieved  it is time to step up efforts to promote  a unified research area where  researchers scientific knowledge and  technology can circulate freely  on space matters ministers will scale up  measures to mitigate the risks from  space debris to space infrastructures  such as galileo and copernicus
 

